# The PATHWAY - BONANZA's map between courses (wave 8b, SPEC.md 128.19.5).
# A PROTOTYPE (the owner, 2026-11-15: "the pathway itself will be a prototype,
# probably; we'll flesh out exact course icons, exact pathway, etc as we make
# courses"). The ball ROLLS across it; each node is a 1-tile finish whose exit
# is the node's number, and rolling onto an OPEN node plays its course. Each
# node's SIGN is a crystal ball beside it: empty locked, a ring open, a tick
# done (S and G are 8c's medals). The clock by the start shows the lives.
course PATH "The Pathway"
width  64
ball   rubber
pathway
music  fairway                              # (the title is the face's; 8b.10 gives the pathway its own)

floor rect   4  4 15 15  flat 0             # the green the nodes stand on (down the screen: x is wx - wy)
start  5  5

clock  5  8                                 # the lives left, one digit (no countdown here)
# (five nodes: a window holds 6 lanes at most, 128.12.4.6 - the five signs and
# the lives' digit; PEAK waits for a pathway that scrolls, or the HUD band)

# node N COURSE wx wy sign sx sy
node 0 FIRST   6  6  sign  6  5
node 1 TRIAL   8  8  sign  8  7
node 2 MILL   12  8  sign 12  7
node 3 PLAY    8 12  sign  8 11
node 4 MOON   11 11  sign 11 10

# edge N EXIT M: a finish of node N's course through EXIT opens node M
edge 0 0 1
edge 1 0 2                                  # TRIAL's back goal cell ...
edge 1 1 3                                  # ...and its front one (exit 1, 128.19.4): a branch
edge 2 0 4
edge 3 0 4                                  # the branch joins again
